  "notes": "Measured on the 777-300ER (B-16723, right side) and checked on the 787-10 (B-17807, left). The A321neo and A330 carry the same scheme; winglets/sharklets not checked. The far side's details (and whether any Chinese title appears) not checked. Colors by eye. The Hello Kitty and Star Alliance aircraft are separate liveries. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on B-16717 (777-300ER, right side): the title agrees (0.159 to 0.306); the sweep's forward edge re-measured as a curve against the window line (it ran about 0.7 m forward mid-height), the pinstripe and belly split drawn as curves.",
  "history": "Replaces Skyarium v1's approximation. EVA's green-and-orange Evergreen scheme, in this form with the dark green belly and the light-green aft sweep, has been standard since the 2010s; the exact year isn't confirmed here, so `from` is left out."
